    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This is a WordPress plugin version of the program &#8220;Responsive Mailform&#8221; that is available for free on my website. ( http://www.1-firststep.com/archives/462 )</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Install the plugin &#8220;Responsive Mailform&#8221; in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Select &#8220;Contact Us&#8221; <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> &#8220;Add New Responsive Email Form&#8221;, set the &#8220;Administrator Email Address&#8221; and save the page.</li>\n<li>Copy the shortcode displayed on page 3 above and paste it on the page where you want to place the email form.</li>\n<li>Try sending a test yourself and if the thank you page appears and the email is delivered, then it&#8217;s OK.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "<p>Details on how to set up and customize are explained on the following page: https://www.1-firststep.com/archives/16638</p>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>9.0</h4>\n<p>Completely renewed. First update in about 10 years.<br />\nUpdated to the same level as the &#8220;Responsive Mailform&#8221;(standard version).</p>\n<h4>1.4</h4>\n<p>Bug fix about furigana empty.</p>\n<h4>1.3</h4>\n<p>Bug fix about mysql_real_escape_string.</p>\n<h4>1.2</h4>\n<p>Bug fix about DateTimePicker.</p>\n<h4>1.1</h4>\n<p>Bug fix about jQuery conflict.</p>\n<h4>1.0</h4>\n<p>New Release.</p>\n"
    },
